  "chapter": 3,
  "sortOrder": 55003,
  "verseCount": 17,
  "aliases": [
    "2 Tim",
    "2Tim",
    "2 Ti",
    "2Ti"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:3:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "This know also, that in the last days perilous times shall come.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 3:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:3:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:3:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "For men shall be lovers of their own selves, covetous, boasters, proud, blasphemers, disobedient to parents, unthankful, unholy,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 3:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:3:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:3:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Without natural affection, trucebreakers, false accusers, incontinent, fierce, despisers of those that are good,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 3:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:3:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:3:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Traitors, heady, highminded, lovers of pleasures more than lovers of God;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 3:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:3:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:3:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Having a form of godliness, but denying the power thereof: from such turn away.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 3:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:3:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:3:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "For of this sort are they which creep into houses, and lead captive silly women laden with sins, led away with divers lusts,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 3:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:3:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:3:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Ever learning, and never able to come to the knowledge of the truth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 3:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:3:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:3:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Now as Jannes and Jambres withstood Moses, so do these also resist the truth: men of corrupt minds, reprobate concerning the faith.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 3:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:3:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:3:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "But they shall proceed no further: for their folly shall be manifest unto all men, as theirs also was.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 3:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:3:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:3:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "But thou hast fully known my doctrine, manner of life, purpose, faith, longsuffering, charity, patience,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 3:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:3:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:3:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Persecutions, afflictions, which came unto me at Antioch, at Iconium, at Lystra; what persecutions I endured: but out of them all the Lord delivered me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 3:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:3:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:3:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Yea, and all that will live godly in Christ Jesus shall suffer persecution.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 3:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:3:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:3:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "But evil men and seducers shall wax worse and worse, deceiving, and being deceived.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 3:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:3:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:3:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "But continue thou in the things which thou hast learned and hast been assured of, knowing of whom thou hast learned them;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 3:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:3:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:3:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "And that from a child thou hast known the holy scriptures, which are able to make thee wise unto salvation through faith which is in Christ Jesus.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 3:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:3:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:3:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "All scripture is given by inspiration of God, and is profitable for doctrine, for reproof, for correction, for instruction in righteousness:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 3:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:3:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:3:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "That the man of God may be perfect, throughly furnished unto all good works.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 3:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:3:17"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
